# Portuguese: the rules the formant voice speaks it by (docs/tts.md,
# "Other languages"). European Portuguese, from its spelling, with the unstressed endings reduced. Stress: the second-last syllable, the last after l, r, z, i or u, and wherever an accent says.
name Portuguese
stress penult
last-if-ends lrziu
unstressed 2
vowels aeiouáéíóúâêôãõà
weak o a os as um uma de do da dos das em no na nos nas e ou que se me te lhe por para com ao à

